goscape (documentation hub) — third-party notices and attribution
=================================================================

This branch carries documentation and the tooling that builds the documentation
site. The engine itself lives on the `rev-N` branches, each of which has its own
NOTICE covering the code it ports.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Lost City — Engine-TS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

goscape is a Go rewrite of the Lost City TypeScript RuneScape server
(https://github.com/LostCityRS/Engine-TS). The documentation here describes that
port and quotes Engine-TS file and line references throughout; the porting
tracker and lessons are written against it directly.

Engine-TS is licensed under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Lost City.
The full text is reproduced in the NOTICE file on each `rev-N` branch.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Zensical
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The documentation site is built with Zensical (https://github.com/zensical/
zensical), MIT licensed. `overrides/main.html` extends a Zensical theme
template; only the override itself is part of this repository.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
mike
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Per-revision versioning of the published site uses mike
(https://github.com/jimporter/mike), by way of the Zensical fork pinned in
requirements.txt. mike is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License,
Copyright (c) 2017-2026, Jim Porter.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Rendered game assets
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

`overlays/rev-*/player/items/icons/` contains item icons rendered from the
pinned Lost City content trees by this repository's own rasterizer, and the
per-revision reference pages are generated from the same content. The underlying
game data and its visual designs originate with Jagex Ltd.; they are reproduced
here only to document what each revision of the engine serves. No affiliation
with or endorsement by Jagex is claimed.
